==English==
{{was wotd|2020|January|20}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Chapéu Masculino, Acervo do Museu Paulista da USP (6).jpg|thumb|A [[Panama hat]] with a [[grosgrain]] [[band#Noun|band]].{{refn|group=n|name=n1|From the collection of the Museu Paulista or {{w|Museu do Ipiranga}} in [[São Paulo]], [[Brazil]].}} Grogram is a type of grosgrain made up of a [[mixture]] of [[silk]], and [[mohair]] or [[wool]].]]

{{PIE root|en|ǵerh₂}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|gros-grain|t=coarse grain, a strong fabric}}, from {{m|fr|gros|t=coarse}} + {{m|fr|grain|t=grain}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵerh₂-|t=to grow old, mature}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=81698|date=1900|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> The word is a {{doublet|en|grosgrain|nocap=1}} which was borrowed later.

